  title: 'Introduction of Public Health Policies (1900s-1930s) '
  info: 'To combat diseases like malaria and tuberculosis, the colonial government
    implemented sanitation measures, vaccination programs, and clean water initiatives.
    The Medical Registration Ordinance (1905) ensured only qualified doctors could
    practice.  '
